How Splunk Work


Data Collection: Splunk gathers data from various sources like
two webservers, applications and network devices


Data 'rdeing ASplunk organizes and stores this data efficiently
in a compressed format for faster searching and retrieval

Search and Analysis: Splunk allows users to search and
analyze this data using a powerful query language called search
processing language (SPL).
Visualization and Reporting: Splunk can present data in
reports and dashboards for easy comprehension. This allows users
to see trends and patterns visually.
Alerts and Actions: Splunk can be configured to set up alerts
based on specific data patterns. This enables proactive identification
and resolution of potential problems
Splunk architecture
There are three primary components
1. Forwarders
collect the data and forward
